    "result_text": "The full test suite is green \u2014 `AcceptanceTest` is the only test class, and both its tests pass.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe requirement: return `contactPreference = 'EMAIL'` when an owner has an email, otherwise `'PHONE'`. This is a derived, read-only field on the owner response returned by `GET /api/owners/{id}` (and the create/list responses, which share the same DTO mapping).\n\nTwo changes:\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a read-only `contactPreference` string property to the `Owner` schema, so `OwnerDto` (generated at build time) carries the field.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added a MapStruct `@Mapping` on `toOwnerDto` that derives it via an expression, mirroring the existing derived fields (`membershipLevel`, `locality`):\n   ```java\n   owner.getEmail() != null && !owner.getEmail().isBlank() ? \"EMAIL\" : \"PHONE\"\n   ```\n   This uses the same \"email present\" test as the existing `MembershipLevel` helper for consistency.\n\nNo new OfficeFloor functions or YAML were needed \u2014 the value flows through the existing `RespondWithOwner` \u2192 `OwnerMapper` path. `Tests run: 2, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` / `BUILD SUCCESS`.",
